From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:04:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] runtime: give the pad a menu mode, a precise cursor and
 the pad used last

When the game shows its cursor (the test rt_host_cursor already makes)
the pad is in menu mode: Cross and the right trigger click, the left
trigger right clicks, Circle is Escape and Square is the game's
inventory key (i, slot6). In play Square opens the inventory too, so
reload moves to the touchpad and the Xbox share button, and the quest
log (l) goes on L3, the one spare every pad has, the Sense pair
included. Create stays on the character sheet (c). The d-pad keeps
1 to 4 in menus: dialogue answers are number keys and the game binds
the arrows to movement. A release always sends what its press sent, so
a button held across a mode change cannot leave a key stuck, and
entering a menu lifts the movement keys the left stick held.

In menus both sticks drive the cursor through a radial dead zone and a
power curve, slow near the centre for inventory slots and fast at the
rim, in client pixels so a slow step is not lost to rounding on a
scaled screen, and scaled by real elapsed time rather than whole
milliseconds. The left stick runs at half speed. The move goes out as
a warp so the Mac pointer and the host's virtual pointer follow it.
Look in play is unchanged. controls.txt takes menu.<button>= for menu
targets, none to unbind, and cursor_speed, cursor_power, cursor_dead
and cursor_left; RT_PAD_* environment variables override it.

Every connected pad is open and the one with a fresh press or stick
push drives, so a gamepad and the Sense pair both work without
reconnecting. Each button is logged once per mode with its target.
